#: ../../source/installation/running.rst:3
msgid "Running Your App"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/running.rst:9
msgid ""
"A CodeIgniter 4 app can be run in a number of different ways: hosted on a"
" web server, using virtualization, or using CodeIgniter's command line "
"tool for testing. This section addresses how to use each technique, and "
"explains some of the pros and cons of them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/running.rst:13
msgid ""
"You should always be careful about the case of filenames. Many developers"
" develop on case-insensitive file systems on Windows or macOS. However, "
"most server environments use case-sensitive file systems. If the file "
"name case is incorrect, code that works locally will not work on the "
"server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/running.rst:19
msgid ""
"If you're new to CodeIgniter, please read the :doc:`Getting Started "
"</intro/index>` section of the User Guide to begin learning how to build "
"dynamic PHP applications. Enjoy!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/running.rst:26
msgid "Initial Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/running.rst:29
msgid "Configure for Your Site URIs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/running.rst:31
msgid "Open the **app/Config/App.php** file with a text editor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/running.rst:33
msgid "$baseURL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/running.rst:34
msgid ""
"Set your base URL to ``$baseURL``. If you need more flexibility, the "
"baseURL may be set within the :ref:`.env <dotenv-file>` file as "
"``app.baseURL = 'http://example.com/'``. **Always use a trailing slash on"
" your base URL!**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/running.rst:38
msgid ""
"If you don't set the ``baseURL`` correctly, in development mode, the "
"debug toolbar may not load properly and web pages may take considerably "
"longer to display."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/running.rst:42
msgid "$indexPage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/running.rst:43
msgid ""
"If you don't want to include **index.php** in your site URIs, set "
"``$indexPage`` to ``''``. The setting will be used when the framework "
"generates your site URIs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/running.rst:46
msgid ""
"You may need to configure your web server to access your site with a URL "
"that does not contain **index.php**. See :ref:`CodeIgniter URLs <urls-"
"remove-index-php>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/running.rst:50
msgid "Configure Database Connection Settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/running.rst:52
msgid ""
"If you intend to use a database, open the **app/Config/Database.php** "
"file with a text editor and set your database settings. Alternately, "
"these could be set in your **.env** file. See :ref:`Database "
"Configuration <database-config-explanation-of-values>` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/running.rst:58
msgid "Set to Development Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/running.rst:60
msgid ""
"If it is not on the production server, set ``CI_ENVIRONMENT`` to "
"``development`` in **.env** file to take advantage of the debugging tools"
" provided. See :ref:`setting-development-mode` for the detail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/running.rst:64
msgid ""
"In production environments, you should disable error display and any "
"other development-only functionality. In CodeIgniter, this can be done by"
" setting the environment to \"production\". By default, the application "
"will run using the \"production\" environment. See also :ref"
":`environment-constant`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/running.rst:70
msgid "Set Writable Folder Permission"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/running.rst:72
msgid ""
"If you will be running your site using a web server (e.g., Apache or "
"nginx), you will need to modify the permissions for the **writable** "
"folder inside your project, so that it is writable by the user or account"
" used by your web server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/running.rst:80
msgid "Checking PHP ini Settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/running.rst:84
msgid ""
"`PHP ini settings`_ change the behaviors of PHP. CodeIgniter provides a "
"command to check important PHP settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/running.rst:93
msgid ""
"The *Recommended* column shows the recommended values for production "
"environment. They may differ in development environments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/running.rst:97
msgid ""
"If you cannot use the spark command, you can use "
"``CheckPhpIni::run(false)`` in your controller."
msgstr ""

