#: ../../source/installation/running.rst:535
msgid "Bootstrapping the App"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/running.rst:537
msgid ""
"In some scenarios, you will want to load the framework without actually "
"running the whole application. This is particularly useful for unit "
"testing your project, but may also be handy for using third-party tools "
"to analyze and modify your code. The framework comes with two separate "
"bootstrap scripts specifically for these scenarios:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/running.rst:542
msgid ""
"**system/Test/bootstrap.php**: This script is used primarily for unit "
"testing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/running.rst:543
msgid ""
"**system/util_bootstrap.php**: This script is used for other scripts that"
" need access to the framework. It is recommended for use in scripts that "
"are not part for testing as this will NOT fail gracefully if an exception"
" is thrown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/running.rst:547
msgid ""
"Most of the paths to your project are defined during the bootstrap "
"process. You may use pre-defined constants to override these, but when "
"using the defaults be sure that your paths align with the expected "
"directory structure for your installation method."
msgstr ""

